# ── 3. Event ⊥ Situation (occurrent vs configuration; NO single-field harvest) ───
# The Event/Situation contrast is not stated in a single harvestable annotation
# field; it is a doc-section/foundation harvest over the occurrent structure. This
# candidate therefore omits BOTH logic:candidateFormalizes and
# logic:candidateSourceField (never a half-link). Its sourceHash is the sha256 of
# logic:Event's skos:definition. Enforced by the native DL coherence gate.

logic:cqEventSituationDisjointHolds
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "event/situation disjointness holds"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The positive competency case the event/situation disjointness axiom must satisfy: an individual typed logic:Event and NOT logic:Situation (a perdurant occurrence composed of temporal parts) stays coherent — it is not forced to owl:Nothing — because an occurrence that unfolds in time is not the static configuration a situation records."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:cqEventSituationClashRejected
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "event/situation clash is rejected"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The negative countermodel the event/situation disjointness axiom must respect: an individual typed BOTH logic:Event and logic:Situation is a violation — the native DL coherence gate forces it to owl:Nothing, because logic:Event owl:disjointWith logic:Situation is asserted. A thing that is at once an unfolding occurrence and the static configuration a situation records is not an admissible model. The boundary the occurrent/configuration distinction enforces."@x-gmeow-english .

