# ── 4. Entity sortal covering (OWL-projection-only, NON-monotone) ────────────────
# Every gmeow:Entity is one of {Agent, InformationObject, PhysicalObject,
# SocialObject}. This covering is realized only in the OWL projection as an
# owl:unionOf and is DISCLOSED in the loss ledger; the native monotone chase does
# NOT enforce disjunctive covering. NO harvest back-link (the covering is not a
# single-field annotation). Category: necessary condition; risk: projection-only.

logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringHolds
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "entity sortal covering holds"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The positive competency case the entity-sortal covering must satisfy: a gmeow:Entity that is one of the four sortals (gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject) is covered by the owl:unionOf — no gap. Realized in the OWL-DL projection; it is the well-formed case the covering disjunction admits."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringGapRejected
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "entity sortal covering gap is rejected"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The negative countermodel the entity-sortal covering must respect: a gmeow:Entity typed into NONE of the four sortals violates the owl:unionOf covering in the OWL-DL projection — an OWL reasoner rejects the class-covering gap. HONEST SCOPE: the native monotone StratifiedNAF gate does NOT enforce this disjunctive covering (a disjunction in the head is non-Horn), so this rejection is realized only in the OWL projection, not in the native chase, and is disclosed in the loss ledger accordingly."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:candidateEntitySortalCovering
    a owl:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "every entity is one of the four sortals"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The necessary-condition formalization candidate governing the class covering that every gmeow:Entity is one of {gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject}. Its source is gmeow:Entity's gmeow:howToUse prose, which enumerates the four sortals. The covering is realized ONLY in the OWL projection as an owl:unionOf (a class-covering disjunction); it is NON-monotone and is disclosed in the loss ledger — the native monotone StratifiedNAF chase does NOT enforce a disjunctive head, so this is projection-only, not natively enforced. It carries NO harvest back-link (the covering is a doc-level enumeration, not a single harvestable axiom field). Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringHolds) and a negative case (logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringGapRejected); logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that gmeow:howToUse text for drift detection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:candidateSourceHash "sha256:349511ccdf3a10b7ce908e62ee66b4102b0469b4b54b191148d817380a8b96ae"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateExtractionProvenance "read from gmeow:Entity's gmeow:howToUse annotation, which enumerates the four sortals (Agent, InformationObject, PhysicalObject, SocialObject); the covering is realized in the OWL projection (owl:unionOf), is non-monotone, and is disclosed in the loss ledger — NOT natively enforced (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateScope "covering: every gmeow:Entity is one of {Agent, InformationObject, PhysicalObject, SocialObject}"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateContract logic:StratifiedNAFProfile ;
