# ── 6. Deliberate SocialObject ∩ InformationObject overlap (reviewed non-assertion) ─
# The one preserved overlap: gmeow:SocialObject and gmeow:InformationObject are
# deliberately NOT asserted disjoint (a myth is legitimately both social and
# informational). This candidate governs that explicit, reviewed non-assertion.
# Category: deliberate overlap; risk: advisory. Its negative case is the
# countermodel showing why the overlap must be preserved.

logic:cqSocialInformationOverlapHolds
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "social/information overlap holds"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The positive competency case the deliberate social/information overlap must satisfy: an individual typed BOTH gmeow:SocialObject and gmeow:InformationObject — a founding myth that is at once socially sustained and information-bearing — stays coherent and is NOT forced to owl:Nothing, precisely because no disjointness between the two is asserted. The overlap the top-sortal partition deliberately preserves."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:cqSocialInformationOverlapDisjointRejected
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "social/information disjointness is rejected"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The negative countermodel that explains WHY the social/information overlap must be preserved: IF gmeow:SocialObject were wrongly asserted owl:disjointWith gmeow:InformationObject, then a founding myth typed as both would be forced to owl:Nothing by the coherence gate — collapsing a legitimate model. The rejected disjointness is the mistake this deliberate non-assertion guards against; asserting it is the boundary the partition must NOT cross."@x-gmeow-english .

