    skos:definition "The equivalence-definition formalization candidate governing logic:falsehoodIsRefutedClaim: to carry gmeow:claimModality gmeow:refuted is exactly to be a gmeow:StandpointClaim that necessarily denies its proposition (gmeow:polarityDeny ∧ gmeow:modalForceNecessary = □¬). This pins 'falsehood = refuted StandpointClaim' as a frame-relative configuration, never a global truth flag, and ties the legacy five-value modality twin to its canonical axes. Realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection (biconditional), non-monotone, disclosed in the loss ledger — NOT natively enforced. Harvested from gmeow:refuted's skos:definition. Accepted through review with a positive case (logic:cqFalsehoodRefutedHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFalsehoodRefutedGlobalTruthRejected)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:candidateSourceHash "sha256:5a0209094cea0065b721afa45f2bda0dacaf1b8c659bf77f5c52c7632f6b0b0e"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateExtractionProvenance "hand-harvested from gmeow:refuted's skos:definition, which states the standpoint DENIES the proposition (□¬, settled-false-in-frame) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateScope "equivalence: gmeow:claimModality gmeow:refuted ⟺ StandpointClaim with polarityDeny ∧ modalForceNecessary"^^xsd:string ;
